# Shell scripts and workflow YAML must keep LF endings on every platform: CRLF
# breaks a script's shebang and makes bash choke on `set -euo pipefail` when
# GitHub's Linux runners execute it, and this repository is developed on
# Windows (where the Rust sources are CRLF, which rustc accepts either way).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Test goldens are raw binary dumps (little-endian f64 arrays, int16 sample
# streams, int8 T-values), regenerated by scripts/. Left to Git's own text
# detection a golden whose bytes happen to contain 0D 0A would be normalized on
# commit, so the committed fixture would no longer be the reference output and
# the test would quietly compare against a different file.
*.bin binary
*.f64 binary
